  "scope": [
    "Captured start executes as a Fiber C-root callback with immutable RAW receiver and cached target selection.",
    "RAW and the result tail each own the Closure. The outer start owns the original buffer, the C handler owns its copy, and waiting inner APIs borrow the receiver without retaining another copied buffer.",
    "Actual outer start buffers, runner headers, sites and caller chains authenticate both initial and saved core continuations; marker deletion cannot fall back to ordinary start admission.",
    "Inner start traces have no file or line site; outer frames retain the real callsite. Status, target-entry names, body exception identity and pre-entry argument unwind retain their actual continuations.",
    "Last RAW retirement can release the Closure and receiver before the original argument destructor. Shared-capture nested direct calls retain distinct source-site ownership."
  ],
